iew (feature 19 must quote Dirda's 'confides in the reader' line it currently omits), [650] for sound patterning, Roberts and Steering ch.1 for names, the [462] note for 'no name till late'. (5) Resolve the self-contradictions: feature 12's absolute anti-archaism rule against the same Elfland page's 'a perfect distancer' [803] and 'archaisms are not essential' [805] — state the rule as Le Guin states it (a distancer, used sparingly), not as a ban; feature 12's 'And' limb now VERIFIED via [114]; feature 8's rule against 'Only in lesser matters is realistic detail used' [827] — state both and resolve by register; the OpenAlex stylometry negative no longer reproduces (3 and 2 hits today) — say 'to be read', not 'none'. (6) The verbless-record rule rests on one sentence of her own prose [884] — flag SINGLE. (7) Copyright hygiene: the four kept rows with a finder quote over twelve words ([808], [896], [900], [903]) are cited by index only; the verifier notes holding 63–90-word passages ([739], [787], [741], [731], [732]) are never copied. (8) State in the Coverage that the random second-verifier sample writing alt remains OWED, and that the critic's FIND angles (academic-3, voice-3, record-register-2, primary-measure-2) were REFUSED under the owner's stopping rule and are carried as S12 open items (primary-measure-2 = the owner's purchase decision)."
